@reporter Thanks for your update.

I guess the reason of new issue is VM configuration. To my understanding, current VM configuration shows 16 cores /16 threads CPU based on actual 8 cores / 16 threads CPU.

To achieve better performance, when OpenVINO uses only one thread on one CPU core, each CPU core runs OpenVINO workload on only one thread now. This feature is enabled after 2023.0.1 and cause different behavior. 

Could you change VM configuration to 8 cores / 16 threads which each socket has 4 cores / 8 threads? If yes, please try OpenVINO nightly builds [02/11](https://<redacted-host>/repositories/openvino/packages/nightly/2025.1.0-18141-b0a120c9684/openvino_toolkit_windows_2025.1.0.dev20250211_x86_64.zip) with configuration `-hint none -nstreams 1 -nthreads 16 -load_config hy_config.json`. The configuration of `hy_config.json` is following:
```
{
        "CPU":
        {"ENABLE_HYPER_THREADING":"YES"}
}
```

@reporter Thanks for your information. 

1. Could you share the performance number of `benchmark_app -hint none -nstreams 1 -nthreads 8 -t 10 -m C:\OpenVINO\test\intel\face-detection-0206\FP16\face-detection-0206.xml"` on your VM platform with key OpenVINO versions?
2. The behavior of `benchmark_app -t 10 -m "C:\OpenVINO\test\intel\face-detection-0206\FP16\face-detection-0206.xml"` is same as `benchmark_app -t 10 -m "C:\OpenVINO\test\intel\face-detection-0206\FP16\face-detection-0206.xml" -hint throughput`. It looks like VM cannot support tbb setting for second socket. We cannot reproduce this issue on bare metal platform with dual socket CPUs.

@reporter Thanks for your update. The crash of "-nstreams 1 -nthreads 8" is same issue as throughput hint when tbbbind configuration is for socket 1.

Since the original issue about running on 2 socket is fixed, could we close this ticket. 

For performance drop issue, could you create another issue? It is better if you can check the performance with bare metal machine.
